{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Compiles cleanly now — fresh `main.pdf` (628 KB), zero undefined citations, zero LaTeX warnings.\n\n**result:** Fixed two issues blocking the build in `tagseq2tagseq/paper/` (note: it's `paper/`, not `papers/`) — the paper now compiles cleanly with latexmk.\n\nWhat was broken:\n\n1. **`bib/refs.bib` had 10 `% FLAG: ...` comment lines inside bib entries.** BibTeX doesn't support `%` comments, so each one killed its entry and cascaded into 263 undefined citations. I moved each comment to just after its entry's closing brace, where BibTeX ignores it — the flag notes are all preserved.\n2. **`sections/03_method.tex` had bare underscores in two `\\todo{}` notes** (`mask_*.png`, `density_aware_*.png`), which is a math-mode error in text. Escaped them as `\\_`.\n\nYour VSCodium LaTeX setup itself was fine — these were content errors, so hitting build in the editor should work again now.\n\nFour cosmetic BibTeX warnings remain if you ever want to tidy them: `gao2021lmeval` uses an entry type `plainnat` doesn't know, `bisk2020piqa` has both `volume` and `number`, and `priem2022openalex`/`taylor2022galactica` have an empty `journal`/`booktitle`. None affect the build.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq","dirty_fingerprint":"6d313a20ffa6f60d087390e39c00db351f6b5657aa502102294314690a707c10","head":"ec8cf5a8fa18aebcaa603afea1c48d53d767d4c9","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/tagseq2tagseq.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:7d8f7607-02f1-48d0-b059-74bc70bed0eb","seq":98},"id":"ev1-3549fe7012aad53bb19b111a519be4c60efa27e6dfc4ec5d3a98ee317d7993f8","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-11T02:20:10.082Z","producer":{"model":"claude-fable-5","session_id":"7d8f7607-02f1-48d0-b059-74bc70bed0eb","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.227","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users